---
// Placeholder about page, written from what Shreya has shared so far.
// TODO(Shreya): rewrite in your own words; add a photo of yourself if you want one.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="About" description="Who cooks here, and how a recipe earns its place on Back of the Fridge.">
  <article class="wrap about">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Hi, I'm <span class="script">Shreya.</span></h1>
      <p class="byline script">a busy mom who cooks on Sundays</p>
    </header>

    <div class="cols">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          I work full time, I have a little one at home, and Sunday is the one day I really cook. Back of the Fridge is
          where I write those Sundays down.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every prep starts with what's already in the fridge and pantry, not a shopping list. I look at the week ahead
          (late meetings, guests, a festival) and plan around it. Then it's one long cooking session, with the oven,
          stovetop and Instant Pot all going at once, and a stack of labeled containers at the end.
        </p>
        <p>
          The food is whatever we actually eat: palak paneer next to a black bean soup, dumplings baked into a coconut
          curry, Mediterranean rice bowls. Mostly vegetarian, never fussy, and it has to taste good on a Thursday.
        </p>

        <h2 id="how">How a recipe gets here</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>The idea.</strong> Sometimes it's family food, sometimes something I saw, and sometimes I ask AI what to do with half a cabbage and a block of paneer.</li>
          <li><strong>I cook it.</strong> In my kitchen, with my groceries, on a real Sunday.</li>
          <li><strong>I fix what didn't work.</strong> Timings, spice, what went soggy by day three. Those notes go on the recipe under "What I changed."</li>
          <li><strong>I photograph it.</strong> My own photos, of my own food.</li>
          <li><strong>Then it goes up</strong> with the date I tested it. If I haven't cooked it, it isn't here.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Why I'm building it this way</h2>
        <p>
          I'm a data scientist, and I'm working on an assistant that plans a Sunday prep from whatever you have in your
          fridge: tell it or show it what's there, and it builds the week. The recipes on this site are what it will learn
          from, so every one needs to be something a real person cooked and would make again. It gets taught by a kitchen,
          not by the internet.
        </p>
        <p>
          Recipes inspired by someone else's are rewritten in my own words, after I've made them my way, and credited.
          Nutrition, where it's shown, is an estimate, and it's labeled that way on purpose.
        </p>
        <p>
          Say hi at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or on <a href={site.pinterest}>Pinterest</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="side" aria-label="House rules">
        <p class="eyebrow">House rules</p>
        <ul>
          <li><span class="n">1</span>Cooked in my kitchen before it's posted</li>
          <li><span class="n">2</span>My own photos</li>
          <li><span class="n">3</span>Honest notes on what I changed</li>
          <li><span class="n">4</span>Every container gets a day: fridge or freezer</li>
          <li><span class="n">5</span>Nutrition is labeled "estimated"</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 72px"><Signup /></div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head { padding: 56px 0 8px; }
  .page-head h1 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 4.6rem); }
  .page-head h1 .script { color: var(--pop); }
  .byline { font-size: 1.4rem; color: var(--ink-2); margin-top: -6px; }
  .cols { display: grid; gap: 48px; margin-top: 24px; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr 300px; gap: 72px; } }
  .prose ol li::marker { color: var(--pop); }
  .side { align-self: start; padding: 26px; background: var(--band); color: var(--band-ink); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .side { position: sticky; top: 96px; } }
  .side .eyebrow { color: var(--band-ink); opacity: 0.65; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .side ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .side li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr; font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .side .n { font-family: var(--display); font-style: italic; font-weight: 700; color: #f0a283; font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 100, 'WONK' 1; }
</style>
